From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 92/92] cuda,tp: tune sm_121 x3gm v3 defaults and skip idle
 RoCE CQ polling

Update x3gm's v3_default variant selection from .{ .gu = .{ 4, 1 }, .dn = 9 }
to .{ .gu = .{ 5, 3 }, .dn = 9 }, selecting the 16-warp KS=4 LEAN gate/up
instances (v3_variants[5] for shared rotated input and v3_variants[3] for dual
inputs) alongside down variant 9 on sm_121 when TF_DSV41_GM_V3=1 is enabled.
Across 2048- and 4096-row uniform and Zipf routing microbenchmarks on GB10,
these 16-warp KS=4 LEAN variants beat v2 by 1.5%-3.7% (whereas the prior
.{ 4, 1 } default regressed up to 8.2% on GB10) with bit-exact outputs.

In fabric/tp/roce.zig, guard proxyLoop's periodic wire.reap() call with
!r.linkIdle() so an idle proxy thread does not hammer ibv_poll_cq when zero
sends are in flight, and extend idle_spins from 20_000_000 to 50_000_000 so
the proxy stays awake across short inter-burst gaps between speculative verify
and draft rounds before sleeping.

Includes host unit tests in exl3_block_exl3.zig and roce_inflight_test.zig
that fail on unpatched main.
